28073996154618,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":50.9,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.03099592391724208,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.16895182784378648,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.1089281160053922,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.03481,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":23.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"UroGen Pharma Ltd., a biotechnology company, engages in the development and commercialization of solutions for urothelial and specialty cancers. It offers RTGel, a novel proprietary polymeric biocompatible, reverse thermal gelation hydrogel technology; Mitomycin a generic drug used off-label as an adjuvant chemotherapy for the treatment of low-grade NMIBC after trans-urethral resection of bladder tumor; Zusduri, a sustained-release formulation of mitomycin for the treatment of non-muscle invasive bladder cancer (NMIBC); and Jelmyto for pyelocalyceal solutions. The company's lead product candidates are UGN-103, which is in phase 3 of clinical trial for intravesical solution; and UGN-104 that is in phase 3 of clinical trial for pyelocalyceal solution designed for the treatment of several forms of non-muscle invasive urothelial cancer that include low-grade upper tract urothelial cancer and low-grade intermediate risk NMIBC. It is also developing UGN-301, UGN-301+UGN 201, and UGN-301+gemcitabine that are in phase 1 of clinical trial for the treatment of high-grade NMIBC. The company has license agreement with Agenus Inc. to develop, make, use, sell, import, and commercialize products of Agenus for the treatment of cancers of the urinary tract via intravesical delivery; and licensing and supply agreement with medac Gesellschaft f\u00fcr klinische Spezialpr\u00e4parate m.b.H. to develop UGN-103 and UGN-104. UroGen Pharma Ltd. was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Princeton, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Elizabeth A. Barrett | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 300 people. Revenue per employee of $366K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 38%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $40K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["UroGen Pharma Ltd. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $1.3B market cap on $110M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +19% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -260% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 89% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $163M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Net dilution runs at 3.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 3.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-4.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"